work fabric_probe_reads_ledger_labels
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 6.0
  reason engine/core/src/fabric_exec.c checks ledger output for the labels Replacement cost and Portfolio value, and engine/core/tests/probe_contract_test.c feeds it 1.23 and 4.56. The labels are kept so the probe still finds them; the probe should check an observed cost or its stated absence, and the test should use a real report.

work kernel_parity_is_not_listed_as_simulation
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 2.0
  reason bonfyre-flashqla compares a fast kernel with a reference on tensors it generates and says so. The work it reports, that two kernels agree and how fast, is done on those tensors; it claims nothing about a model. Left as it is on that reading; a recorded tensor from a model would be a stronger input and none exists here.

