  reason scripts/organ_drift.sh is the one path that checks an installed organ against its build. Several Makefiles still install from their default target (cms and project copy into ~/.bonfyre/bin and re-sign, which changes the digest), so a plain make there reads as drift, and two organs currently do. The tool also does not list distribute, which was installed by hand.

work commercial_records_are_notes_nothing_acts_on
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 9.0
  reason Direction from the operator, 2026-10-10: the financial organs were being exercised on dog food while the estate's real commercial facts sat in the content store as notes. Found there: 9 deals, 6 requests for quotation drafted to named vendors, 2 supplier quotations received (250 and 630 USD), 31 funding work packages, 31 bounties with no stated amount, a stated pledge of 120 USD with no receipt, 4 service leads; and in the estate's working finance store 9 opportunities with 41,564 USD of expected cost and no stated compensation. The finance operator is now certified on those opportunities and bonfyre-finance books reports the rest beside the books. Nothing yet acts on them: the commerce chain holds only 48 observed lots, none of these deals is an exchange in it, a supplier quotation cannot become a commitment, and a pledge cannot be matched to a receipt. Wiring those records into commerce, offer, pay and books is the work.

work experiment_prices_remain_in_the_home_finance_store
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 3.0
  reason ~/.local/share/bonfyre/finance.db still holds ten services priced at millionths of a dollar from old experiments. Nothing is certified on it any more. It should be emptied or archived by its owner.

work nothing_in_the_chain_is_past_listing
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 8.5
  reason The estate's nine real listed opportunities are now exchanges in its commerce chain, each at product and listing, which is all an opportunity record establishes. The next stage for every one is inventory, owned by the seller: confirmed counts and condition. That is what the deals' own next steps say is missing. Until a seller confirms, the chain correctly refuses an offer, a quote, a commitment and a payment for them, and the quote and payment verbs now obey it. Moving any exchange forward takes a fact from outside: a seller's count, a buyer's bid.

work supplier_quotation_cannot_become_a_commitment
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 7.0
  reason Two supplier quotations (250 and 630 USD) are held as draft records. Nothing accepts one: there is no verb that turns a quotation the estate received into a commitment in the commitment store, and the commerce chain models a sale by the estate and not a purchase by it. The seven opportunities that are applications or messages sent are not in the chain either, for the same reason: it has no shape for a service engagement.


work edge_tools_not_deployed_and_account_at_its_daily_limit
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 7.5
  reason Superseded the same day: the worker was removed. The second Cloudflare account answers Browser Rendering and Workers AI directly, so no worker of the estate's own is needed for either. What stands from it: on the first account, Workers AI calls return error 1027, the daily Workers request ceiling its live sites alert on.

work cloudflare_probe_calls_the_wrong_verify_and_reports_configured
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 6.5
  reason The estate's resource view records provider cloudflare as configured while its own probe of /user/tokens/verify failed with HTTP 400. The second account's token is account-owned: /accounts/<id>/tokens/verify answers active, and Workers AI, Vectorize, D1, KV, Queues and Browser Rendering all answer with it. The probe should try the account verify, and a failed probe should not read as configured.

work recall_has_no_reranker
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 6.0
  reason Recall orders by vector distance alone and a loosely worded question misses the passage a close wording finds. Workers AI on the second account answers bge-reranker-base in about a second and bge-m3 embeddings at 1,024 dimensions. A rerank step for recall query was written but not applied or run: sending the estate's private passages to a hosted model needs the operator's say first.

work near_identical_coordination_records
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 3.0
  reason Asking the campaign store about unanswered outreach returns outbound_message 16, 18 and 19 with the same authority paragraph word for word. Repeats are dropped inside one source file but not across records, so one fact fills several result slots. The record store has equivalence families; Recall does not consult them.

work page_state_reader_keeps_the_page_chrome
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 4.0
  reason Reading a script-built page from its embedded state returns every string in it that reads as prose. On the operator's thread that is the conversation and also the host application's own text (feature notes, onboarding instructions), which changes between fetches. Nothing separates the document from the application around it, and who said each turn is not recovered.

work embedder_cannot_see_non_latin_passages
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 5.5
  reason Two passages of the operator's thread, both Chinese trade material, are invisible to the local embedding vocabulary. Recall now keeps them in the word index and reports them instead of failing the build, but they have no vector. The operator has named China, Vietnam and India as markets. A multilingual embedding answers on the estate's second Cloudflare account (bge-m3, 1,024 dimensions); a local one is not installed.

work site_product_face_is_a_baseline_not_a_finish
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 7.5
  reason The site verbs exist and a stranger can now stand a site up; what they give is one page shape. A new site is a single community thread under a masthead: no pages, no navigation that leads anywhere but /community, no theme choice beyond one accent colour, no media, no editing after creation except through the content store's own entry verbs, no publish step that puts a site on the internet, and no delete. The estate's 1,702 newsroom sites show as "profile only" because the verbs read composition from site_program and those sites are drawn another way. Imports bring text and titles: images, authors, categories, comments and links between posts are left behind. Export to WordPress and Frappe is checked by reading the file back with this estate's own readers, not by either system importing it. The page has not been looked at by a person for whether it is good. site check now names dead links, unreadable colours, a missing name, language or viewport and an empty site, and it caught two faults of this work: a trimmed share directory that left the linked community page out, and a page with no declared language. The community page a new site links to is the estate's shared surface, not the site's own: it does not carry the site's name.

work bridges_move_rows_and_text_not_systems
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 7.0
  reason Direction from the operator, 2026-10-10: clients want bridges, Frappe to WordPress and back, Postgres to MySQL and back, and everything in between, with verification. The database bridge moves tables and compares both sides; it does not carry keys, indexes, constraints, views, sequences or procedures, reads whole tables with no resume, and has been run on tables of a few rows. The content bridge carries posts as text between WordPress and Frappe formats; it has never written to a running WordPress or Frappe, and no Frappe document type other than Blog Post and Web Page is read. Nothing bridges WordPress users, WooCommerce orders or Frappe transactions. The estate's surface maturity audit and ast-grep rules are still not what site check runs; it reads the served page and its records only.

work deliverables_must_arrive_whole_not_as_links
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 7.0
  reason Two signals from real outreach say the same thing. A buyer replied that he will not open the links sent and needs photographs attached directly. The operator said the examples sent were repository links, not at the level of the email. Export exists as static pages and object-store mirrors; nothing produces a self-contained file (a PDF or an image set) from a site, a record or a work sample that can ride in a message.

work accepted_requests_stop_at_the_owner
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 5.5
  reason The operator's correction, 2026-10-10: the gaps listed after offers and bookings read as plans to build what the estate already has. They were wired to their owners instead (commitment store, meter and Pay, Finance, the domain organ). What that still does not do: tell the customer (nothing is sent; Outreach and Distribute own sending and are not called), move the Finance opportunity past import (it sits at specified; proposal, authority, customer and payment attestations are not made from the site verbs, and the payment in Pay is not attested to Finance), show a customer their own promise or invoice, or let them pay. A commitment's id is the offer and the time as written, so "14:00" and "2pm" are two different times to it. The demos' other section shapes are still not fragment kinds. site promises does not show whether a promise was discharged.
work shared_address_is_temporary_and_the_live_estate_changes_on_restart
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 7.0
  reason site share gives a site a public address through a quick tunnel: it lasts while this machine is awake, changes every time, and is not the site's own domain. There is no command that puts a site on a named domain. Separately, the estate's own public server runs the resolver binary this work rebuilt; at its next restart the 1,203 newsroom addresses that hold readings will begin answering /mcp and /llms.txt, which they do not today. That is a change to what the estate serves publicly and nobody has decided it; the operator should restart knowingly or hold the build back.

work view_is_proven_in_the_reference_host_not_in_an_assistant
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 4.0
  reason The view completes its handshake with the protocol's own host library, redraws from a delivered tool result and follows the host's theme, in a browser Cloudflare runs. It has not been opened inside ChatGPT, Claude or any other assistant, whose sandboxing and sizing may differ, and the frame did not grow to its content in the reference host.

