  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 2.0
  reason Closed 2026-10-11 for four probes. clean-transcript, paragraph-structure, whisper-semantic and transcript-family-semantic passed only when the output held the sentence the workload fixture is written with, so a real transcript failed them. Each now checks the run against its own input: cleaned words are the transcript's words in order, paragraphed text keeps every source word, the transcript text and its timed segments agree and end inside the audio. Witnessed through Fabric on a spoken recording and a typed transcript. The other probes in fabric_exec.c have not been read for the same fault, and scripts/bonfyre-command-workloads could not be rerun whole on this machine because it needs a packet capture.

work reference_pages_are_eight_of_ninety_three
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 6.0
  reason bonfyre fabric operator reference writes a command's page from its contract, its binding and its latest receipted run, and bonfyre site page publishes it into a manual with grouped pages, find, outline, code sets and previous and next. The earlier reference run covered eight commands; eighty-five had no recorded run in that selected state. Pages ran 390 to 580 words against 1,200 to 3,700 on the command pages of Stripe, Tailwind, Bun, Astro, Supabase and Wrangler fetched that day. No command carried a one-line purpose in the catalog and bound arguments printed as written (<argument-model_path>); those reference-generator gaps have not been reverified in this continuation. Update 2026-10-11: docs/experiences contains the landing page and all six guide drafts. The local-data guide now supplies its inputs and was executed directly from all five shell blocks against the installed Nomic ONNX model: three stored notes, relevant retrieval through both search paths, replacement without duplication, persistence across command processes, deletion and harmless retry. packs/no-simulation/local-data-guide-20261011.json retains the source and binary hashes and observed results. All seven pages were loaded through site page into the isolated .bonfyre-runtime/docs-review-20261011 home, served with manual markup at docs-review.localhost:8913, and listed through MCP; site check reported zero failures. The other five guides still need complete example execution, and fresh-machine model setup, dark mode and desktop/mobile visual review remain unverified. The local-data commands require a preinstalled model and sqlite-vec; this does not establish a packaged SDK release.

