work site_product_copy_ran_older_behavior
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 2.0
  reason Closed locally 2026-10-11. bonfyre site resolved cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/bonfyre-site, a copied executable from 13:07, ahead of the current 19:22 resolver. The request-to-books tutorial displayed $85 but its stored offer had no numeric amount, so acceptance recorded a commitment and opportunity without an invoice. The Makefile now maintains the product name as a relative symlink to the resolver, including replacing an existing copied file, and removes it on clean. make -C cmd/BonfyreWebAddress site-product-witness passed alias checks and the existing site product suite. All eight shell blocks in docs/experiences/request-to-books.md then ran through bonfyre site: an $85 invoice, one tutorial payment, unchanged books on retry, delivered commitment and two journal entries. packs/no-simulation/request-to-books-guide-20261011.json retains those results and source/binary hashes. The revised guide is served in the isolated docs-review home. Together with the local-data walkthrough, two of the six guide drafts now have complete command execution evidence; white-label, audio, migration and models/compression still need it. No installed runtime update, remote deployment, customer message, model-cost execution or real settlement was performed.

work database_bridge_verification_lost_field_boundaries
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 2.0
  reason Closed 2026-10-11. The verifier joined column text with character 31 and substituted NUL for SQL NULL. Different field values could therefore yield identical hash input, and a missing verification destination was created by a read-write attachment. The native bridge now hashes separate nullable column arguments and uses read-only destination attachments during verification and post-copy readback. The expanded existing suite passed separator, NULL/NUL, unchanged-file and missing-destination cases, plus real MariaDB/PostgreSQL round trips and tamper checks. architecture/external/database-bridge.yaff records the existing owner and its limits. All six shell blocks in docs/experiences/integration-and-migration.md passed: two published WordPress posts with a draft excluded, HTML/Frappe/WXR exports, Bonfyre format round trips, five database rows moved and a changed amount detected. packs/no-simulation/migration-guide-20261011.json retains those results. Three of six guide drafts now have executable walkthrough evidence. Actual WordPress/Frappe destination imports, white-label/audio/models guide execution and visual review remain open; aggregate hashes do not establish collision-free equality or a shared database snapshot.

work site_mcp_origin_used_substring_matching
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 2.0
  reason Closed locally 2026-10-11. The site MCP endpoint accepted browser origins containing its hostname anywhere, including a lookalike domain or path, and accepted opaque null origins. It now matches HTTP(S) authorities by host and port, with a named-site allowance for the loopback path endpoint, on GET and POST. The existing site product suite passed valid-origin, lookalike, sibling-site, wrong-port, malformed and null-origin checks alongside scoped keys and write permissions; its optional reference MCP client check was skipped because BONFYRE_MCP_SDK_DIR was unset. All six shell blocks in docs/experiences/white-label-delivery.md passed against a fresh three-site store on port 8926. HTML and MCP readbacks kept each site's content, Tallgrass alone received the enquiry, Fernhollow alone changed its tagline, and foreign or revoked keys were refused. packs/no-simulation/white-label-guide-20261011.json retains the results and hashes. The isolated docs preview was refreshed with the new executable and guide; the live estate and the separate preview on port 8916 were left running. Four of six guide drafts now have executable walkthrough evidence. Audio and models/compression execution, desktop/mobile visual review, finished customer branding, custom domains and per-customer billing isolation remain open.

work recording_workspace_needed_a_full_recording
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 2.0
  reason Advanced 2026-10-11 with the complete 360-second Composing Webb Telescope Images video from NASA, featuring Joseph DePasquale and Alyssa Pagan. The existing ServiceSite recording owner now groups interrupted ASR sentences into complete timed passages, retains source credits and links, plays search results from their timestamps, follows the transcript through playback and viewport resizing, exports the transcript and keeps separate notes for separate moments. A real browser failure on response.blob was fixed with a session-authorized byte-range media endpoint. New Nomic indexes now pair search_document and search_query prefixes; older indexes retain their original query encoding. The real video yields 60 passages, and three questions about brightness, filters and wavelength colors return the relevant passage first and play it after minutes two, four and five. Desktop/mobile interaction checks and screenshots pass, along with the document and recording regressions. All four guide blocks ran verbatim. packs/no-simulation/recording-guide-20261011.json and recording-workspace-20261011 retain receipts, caption comparison, source hashes and browser evidence. Five of six guides now have executable walkthroughs. Models/compression remains; other sites still need their own visual review. The prior 49-second clinic's recognition issue is not declared repaired by this different recording, and general recognition accuracy is not inferred from this run.

work model_guide_needed_physical_roundtrip_measurements
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 2.0
  reason Closed locally 2026-10-11. Model manifest parsing treated JSON object keys as download addresses and could read fields after an empty source array. Registration now decodes JSON, validates before mutation, replaces sources atomically and keeps model identity references. Quant roundtrip used a different in-memory encoder and estimated storage; it now saves BQFP files, uses the shared decoder and counts physical bytes. A pinned MiniLM-L3-v2 download passed its publisher digest. All 55 floating-point tensors and 17,389,824 weights were encoded and recovered: 19,421,016 bytes against 69,559,296 float32 bytes, weighted cosine 0.998609. Independent SLI recovery agrees with the benchmark. All six guide shell blocks passed, including exact recovery of 83 documentation files and incomplete-file refusal. Native manifest, passport, roundtrip, malformed-file and archive regressions passed. packs/no-simulation/models-compression-guide-20261011.json retains measurements and source hashes. All six guides now have executable walkthroughs; full-model inference from compressed weights remains outside this measurement.

